+### #607 — pause/end recurring payments without rewriting history (source, 2026-10-21)
+
+- Source implementation follows owner #482 and the independently reviewed #607 contract: a pause starts on server Vienna today and includes its last day; “Beenden ab” stores the preceding day in the existing inclusive end date. Canonical shifted dates, rhythm anchors, immutable price versions and contract-equivalent amounts remain shared.
+- An additive, hand-authored migration49 retains audited pause intervals. Explicit actions bind the reviewed payment/versions/occurrences/history token inside their transaction; corrupt or bounded-out evidence cannot supply a mutation token. Only future unassigned expected occurrences are suppressed, with assigned and past/manual history retained.
+- Stored reopened obligations use the same action-relative suppression after ordinary booking link loss, including after their due day; raw payment history remains accessible. Detail projection jumps pause intervals and preserves bounded earliest-date ordering. Delete requires positive proof of no lifetime assignment; missing provenance directs the user to ending instead.
+- The existing Undo transaction calls a scoped helper for whole lifecycle actions, current unbranched generations, lifetime-delete redo and overlap/new-obligation refusal. Actual coherent booking-link maintenance retains its existing financial guards and behavior. No generic booking writer, audit replay implementation or old test was changed.
+- Existing payment dialogs expose “Pausieren bis” / “Beenden ab”, preserve reviewed tokens while open, distinguish inclusive legacy editing and protect untouched draft fields during refetch. Existing controls and design touch tokens are reused.
